  "After that swing? Nobody at this table is comfortable. Good. Comfortable is how corners get taken.": [
   666555,
   6065
  ],
  "Mm. Streetlight flickered on that one. It knows.": [
   672870,
   3585
  ],
  "Busted. The Pj’s keeps what it catches.": [
   676705,
   4065
  ],
  "Streetlight’s holding its breath out there. It only does that when it’s real.": [
   681020,
   4280
  ],
  "Frederick Douglass. Taught himself to read when it was forbidden to him, escaped slavery at twenty, and wrote it all down for the world to answer for.": [
   685550,
   6745
  ],
  "Harriet Tubman. She got herself free — then went back some thirteen times for family and strangers alike, and she brought out every single one.": [
   692545,
   8195
  ],
  "Nat Turner. In 1831 he rose in Southampton County and led the deadliest slave rebellion in American history.": [
   700990,
   8270
  ],
  "Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. Twenty-six years old when Montgomery stopped riding the buses — and he led that boycott all 381 days.": [
   709510,
   7200
  ],
  "Sojourner Truth. Born enslaved — and the first Black woman to win a court case against a white man in this country, bringing her own son home.": [
   716960,
   8280
  ],
  "Fannie Lou Hamer. A Mississippi sharecropper who stood before a national convention in 1964 and told the truth until the whole country had to listen.": [
   725490,
   8700
  ],
  "Marcus Garvey. He built the largest Black movement of his age — and put our own ships on the water with the Black Star Line.": [
   734440,
   7400
  ],
  "Ida B. Wells. A mob wrecked her newspaper office for printing the truth about lynching — so she carried that truth north and printed it louder.": [
   742090,
   7225
  ],
  "W.E.B. Du Bois. The first Black man to earn a Ph.D. from Harvard, in 1895 — and he spent ninety-five years writing the record straight.": [
   749565,
   8135
  ],
  "Malcolm X. He remade himself in a prison cell — walked out teaching discipline, dignity, and standing up straight.": [
   757950,
   7090
  ],
  "Angela Davis. A philosopher they put on trial in 1972 — she walked out acquitted, and she has been teaching ever since.": [
   765290,
   9855
  ],
  "Huey P. Newton. In 1966, in Oakland, he co-founded the Black Panther Party — and a neighborhood's protection became a movement.": [
   775395,
   9330
  ],
  "Hold on now. That's Malcolm they just cut. The man told us freedom would come 'by any means necessary' — a spade on a playing card changes none of it.": [
   784975,
   8550
  ],
  "Malcolm X, cut down on a trick. He taught a whole generation to stand up straight — 'by any means necessary' was never a slogan. It was a promise.": [
   793775,
   8300
  ],
